{
  "$comment": "Vendored @/ui manifest, checked by apps/web/scripts/ui-drift.ts (bun run ui:drift). Edit notes, files, excluded and localOnly by hand; let `bun run ui:drift --record` write the blob ids and the generated sections of VENDORED.md. See VENDORED.md for the sync procedure.",
  "upstream": {
    "repo": "https://github.com/garygentry/deck.git",
    "commit": "209c6359336e8a6d70223ed37efcf687421edabc",
    "describe": "deck v0.5.0",
    "defaultRef": "main"
  },
  "docs": "apps/web/src/client/ui/VENDORED.md",
  "scope": {
    "upstream": [
      "apps/web/src/ui/",
      "apps/web/src/styles/",
      "apps/web/components.json",
      "packages/sdk/tailwind/theme.css"
    ],
    "local": [
      "apps/web/src/client/ui/",
      "apps/web/src/client/styles/"
    ]
  },
  "notes": {
    "dropdown-checked": "`checked` is spread only when defined (`exactOptionalPropertyTypes`).",
    "sidebar-text-entry": "The Ctrl/Cmd-B toggle returns early when `isTextEntryTarget(event.target)`, so the chord stays with a focused text field.",
    "style-nonce": "The Radix `Viewport` gets `{...styleNonceProps()}` (its `nonce`; `lib/style-nonce.ts`), because it renders its own `<style>` element that the strict CSP `style-src` blocks without the response's nonce (issue #2). Re-apply on every sync, and wire any newly vendored primitive whose Radix part takes a `nonce` prop.",
    "app-css": "Pulse's Tailwind entry, kept in deck's file order with deck's base rules: `source(\"..\")` on the Tailwind import and an `@source not` for the workbench (no `@source` for deck's runtime modules, which pulse does not have), `theme-pulse.css` instead of `hljs.css`, the token utilities from the vendored `tailwind-theme.css` (deck imports `@deck/sdk/tailwind/theme.css`), no `@fontsource` imports (the faces register from `styles/fonts.ts`), and pulse base rules (heading wrap, focus ring, inline monospace size, app-wide reduced motion).",
    "icons-additions": "Pulse additions: a second `lucide-react` import block and a \"pulse additions\" section at the end of `ICONS` (the shell and views' icons deck lacks). The shell's icons moved to the pulse-only `icons-shell.ts` (spread into `ICONS`, which keeps its type and contents) and `FALLBACK_ICON` with them; evaluating `icons.ts` registers the set with `icon-registry.ts` (pulse-only), so it can load as a lazy chunk.",
    "components-json": "`tailwind.css` points at `src/client/styles/app.css`.",
    "barrel-exports": "No `ConfigGate` or contributed-icon exports (`contributed-icons.ts` is not vendored). Adds the pulse-only exports: `FreshnessStamp`/`FreshnessState`, `commandGroupsFromIndex` (+ `CommandGroupsOptions`, `CommandIndexEntry`, from the pulse-only `lib/command-groups.ts`), the `useDisposable` hook, `isTextEntryTarget`, `export * from \"./status\"`, the StatusTimeline layout helpers (`timelineHeight`, `timelineSegmentRect`, `TimelineLayoutOpts`, `TimelineRect`) for the timeline view's decorations, the pulse-only `TimeSeriesChart` (+ its types), and the TreeView virtualization exports (`TREE_VIEW_VIRTUALIZE_DEFAULTS`, `TreeViewVirtualizeOptions`).",
    "freshness-types": "Imports `FreshnessStamp`/`FreshnessState` from `lib/freshness.ts` (deck imports them from its server contract).",
    "console-prefix": "Console prefix `[deck]` becomes `[pulse]`.",
    "icon-registry": "Resolves names through `lib/icon-registry.ts`: shell icons eager, the rest once the lazy icon chunk loads; an empty same-size svg until then, the fallback glyph if the load fails. Deck's module-contributed SVG icons (`contributed-icons.ts`, v0.5.0) are not taken: pulse has no runtime modules.",
    "facet-default-open": "`defaultOpen ?? false`.",
    "segmented-key-shortcuts": "Optional `keyShortcuts`, set as `aria-keyshortcuts` on every option (the focusable radios).",
    "exact-optional": "Type-only `| undefined` widenings on optional props for `exactOptionalPropertyTypes` (`headingLevel`, `noun`, `role` and `variant`, the `useShowMore` options, `TreeAccessors`, `CommandPalette`'s `search`/`onSearchChange`).",
    "text-entry-guard": "The `/` shortcut's guard is the shared `isTextEntryTarget` (adds contenteditable ancestors; a checkbox no longer blocks it) instead of a local `isEditable`.",
    "pulse-name": "The app name is Pulse (`APP_TITLE = \"Pulse\"`; the hook's doc comment).",
    "dom-text-entry": "Pulse `isTextEntryTarget` (text-like input, textarea, select, contenteditable; narrower than `isEditableTarget`, which also covers buttons and composite widgets).",
    "tree-view-virtualize": "Pulse `virtualize` prop (`@tanstack/react-virtual`; at a visible-row threshold, default 300, the treeitems render flat in a `tree-view-viewport` scroll region with `aria-hidden` spacers, `aria-level`/`aria-setsize`/`aria-posinset` from the model, rows measured as they render, the focused row and the Tab stop kept rendered, keyboard moves over every visible row through `useListNavigation`'s `virtual` option; hysteresis as in deck's `data-table.tsx`; below the threshold the output is deck's); `*` expands every sibling branch and printable keys move by label (type-ahead), both from the model; the row is `flex-wrap` and the meta wrapper is `contents` (deck: `inline-flex min-w-0`), so a caller's meta can take a line of its own (`basis-full`) at narrow widths.",
    "list-navigation-virtual": "Optional `virtual` (`count`, `activeIndex`, `focus(index)`), so moves in a virtualized list run over every item, not only the rendered ones (deck's `focusEdge` covers only Home/End); optional `typeaheadActive()`, while true printable keys (j/k included) are left to the list's type-ahead.",
    "tree-row-position": "`VisibleTreeRow` carries `posInSet`/`setSize`.",
    "stat-tile-absent": "Optional `valueState: \"absent\"` (placeholder text such as \"not reported\" renders small and muted on the neutral tone, whatever `tone` says, so \"no data\" never reads as a headline number) with an optional screen-reader `absentDescription`; the root and the value carry `data-value-state`."
  },
